Given a module $M$ with no repeated factors that is built from a set of modules $\{N_1, \dots, N_k\}$, we establish a method to reconstruct its lattice of submodules using only information about the factors of $M$ and their multiplicities. The reconstruction formula is based on the relationships between the $N_i$'s. Specifically, given the modules $N_i$ up to isomorphism, and given the multiplicities of the $N_i$'s in $M$, we can reconstruct the lattice of submodules of $M$. The formula is as follows:
$$
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{Sub}(M) &\cong \{ \prod_{i=1}^k N_i^{m_i} \mid \text{for all } i \neq j, \text{if } N_i \text{ is a factor of } N_j, \frac{m_i}{m_j} \leq e_{N_i,N_j}, \text{ and } \sum_{i=1}^k m_i = e_{N_i,N_i} \}
\end{align*}
$$
